{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And he took portions from before him, etc.</b> The brothers thought that the reason he was giving them gifts and honoring them was to appease them for the suspicion he had cast upon them as spies, though they were not: 'and Benjamin's portion was multiplied' — because through this suspicion he had brought him into the danger of the journey for nothing. But the truth is that there is a hint here to the future, for thus Rashi explained (Genesis 45:14) 'and he fell upon Benjamin's necks' — that he wept over the Temple that would be built in his portion and was destined to be destroyed. And according to this midrash we may say that this is why Benjamin's portion was multiplied five handbreadths — a hint to the generations, that the Temple would be built in his portion and there would be in it five things in surpassing exaltation, namely: the Shekhinah, the Ark, the Urim and Thummim, prophecy, and fire from heaven; and these were lacking in the Second Temple. A hint to the matter: five times יָד amounts to the number seventy, a hint to the Temple, the eye of the earth, where the session of the seventy of the Sanhedrin would be, and where they would offer seventy bulls against the seventy nations. And concerning this he said, ״אֱלֹהִים יָחְנְךָ בְּנִי״ (Genesis 43:29) — for the Temple possesses an adornment of grace, as it is written (Zechariah 4:7) ״וְהוֹצִיא אֶת הָאֶבֶן הָרֹאשָׁה תְּשֻׁאוֹת חֵן חֵן לָהּ״."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {0 "The word מַשְׂאֹת/מַשְׂאַת is rendered 'portions' following standard usage; חָמֵשׁ יָדוֹת is rendered 'five handbreadths' as a unit of measure."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:20.786723489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}